From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 21:18:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] bitfield: make __bad_mask() a stub for tinycc

field_multiplier() calls the __bad_mask() canary when its argument is
not a contiguous mask; an optimizing compiler inlines the helper into
FIELD_PREP()/FIELD_GET() and the u32_encode_bits() family, sees that the
condition is false for the constant masks and drops the call, so the
extern is never referenced.  tinycc does not inline, keeps the call in
every user (cfg80211, mac80211, ath9k, HD-audio: 25 objects) and fails
the link.  Under __TINYC__ let the canary be an empty static inline, as
seqlock.h already does for its canaries; the compile-time check stays
with the other compilers.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 include/linux/bitfield.h | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/bitfield.h b/include/linux/bitfield.h
index 14f86e455..489600929 100644
--- a/include/linux/bitfield.h
+++ b/include/linux/bitfield.h
@@ -213,8 +213,17 @@
 
 extern void __compiletime_error("value doesn't fit into mask")
 __field_overflow(void);
+#ifdef __TINYC__
+/*
+ * tcc does not inline field_multiplier(): the call to the canary stays in
+ * every caller, so the mask check has to be a run-time no-op here (the
+ * compile-time check is made by the other compilers).
+ */
+static inline void __bad_mask(void) { }
+#else
 extern void __compiletime_error("bad bitfield mask")
 __bad_mask(void);
+#endif
 static __always_inline u64 field_multiplier(u64 field)
 {
 	if ((field | (field - 1)) & ((field | (field - 1)) + 1))
